The files in `rules/` are unmodified. The filter engine in `src/` is an
independent implementation and is not derived from RTK source code.

The rules in `rules-workcell/` are original to this project and are not derived
from RTK. They are kept in a separate directory so that refreshing the vendored
corpus stays a clean copy of `rules/`, and so that provenance is visible without
reading individual files. Both directories are concatenated at build time and a
file name may not appear in both.

Behavioral changes relative to RTK, applied by this engine rather than by
editing the vendored rules:

  * `on_empty` and `match_output` short-circuit messages are suppressed when the
    command exited non-zero, so a failing command is never reported as success.
  * Rules are matched against a normalized command scope produced by
    tree-sitter Bash parsing rather than the raw command string.
  * Only the built-in rule set is loaded. Project-local and user-global rule
    files are deliberately unsupported.
